"Summary of earlier turns:\n- Searched apps/canvas for \"ops-shell\" and \"OpsShell\": not found. Searched \"Shell\": it is the shared component `Shell` imported from \"@dcortex/canvas-ui\" and used by nearly every screen in apps/canvas/src/screens/*.tsx (AccessAdmin, Analytics, ApiKeys, Dashboard, Launchpad, TaskPane, TenantConfig, Usage, UserAdmin, etc.). Most pass logo=consoleLogo(t), brand=consoleBrand(client, t), controls=<ConsoleControls client={client}/>, rail=buildRail(t, id, onNavigate); a few (LeadershipOversight, Roster, VettingQueue, WorkBoard) pass a plain <strong> brand and railItems. Helpers consoleBrand/consoleLogo/ConsoleControls live in apps/canvas/src/ConsoleControls.tsx; its tests are in ConsoleControls.test.tsx.\n- Found the definition: platform/canvas-ui/src/Shell.tsx, `export function Shell({ brand, logo, controls, rail, sidebar, toolbar, children })`. It renders div.shell-root > header.shell-header (div.shell-brand with logo or default leaf logo, then brand; optional div.shell-controls) and div.shell-body > nav.shell-rail (rail items as <a> if href else <button>, class rail-item/active), optional aside.shell-sidebar (class \"collapsed\" when !open), and main.shell-main (toolbar then children). Props: RailItem {id,label,icon,active?,href?,onSelect?}.\n- Read platform/canvas-ui/styles.css (the output was truncated in the display). Shell styles: .shell-root is flex column, height 100vh, overflow hidden; .shell-header 62px tall; .shell-rail 55px wide; .shell-sidebar 280px, collapsing to width 0; .shell-main flex:1, overflow:auto, flex column (the scroll container); .shell-content padding 18px. The same file also holds the console header chrome, review sidebar, toolbar, segmented chips, KPI grid/card, detail panel, Gantt, and the Controller desk (.desk-root) styles. I saw nothing yet that needs changing, and no edits have been made."
